I'm sorry.

481
00:17:24,111 --> 00:17:26,111
I know what you're thinking,

482
00:17:26,111 --> 00:17:29,111
but I won't ride on stilts ever again.

483
00:17:29,111 --> 00:17:31,111
We'll catch up to the village, too.

484
00:17:31,111 --> 00:17:33,111
I don't care how many years it takes us.

485
00:17:34,111 --> 00:17:35,111
Huh?

486
00:17:35,111 --> 00:17:37,111
You made it back!

487
00:17:41,111 --> 00:17:43,111
We brought you a souvenir.

488
00:17:48,111 --> 00:17:49,111
You're hurt.

489
00:17:49,111 --> 00:17:51,111
Are you all right?

490
00:17:51,111 --> 00:17:52,111
Huh?

491
00:17:52,111 --> 00:17:53,111
Aw, this?

492
00:17:53,111 --> 00:17:54,111
It's nothing.

493
00:17:54,111 --> 00:17:55,111
Huh.

494
00:17:55,111 --> 00:17:57,111
Thank you for your help.

495
00:17:57,111 --> 00:17:58,111
Hee-hee!

496
00:18:02,111 --> 00:18:04,111
Is that why you accepted the fight?

497
00:18:04,111 --> 00:18:05,111
Because you wanted to help him?

498
00:18:05,111 --> 00:18:08,111
And here I thought you were just being stupid again.

499
00:18:08,111 --> 00:18:10,111
Man, you're rude.

500
00:18:10,111 --> 00:18:11,111
What?

501
00:18:11,111 --> 00:18:12,111
What's happening?

502
00:18:12,111 --> 00:18:13,111
Guys, I don't like this.

503
00:18:13,111 --> 00:18:14,111
It's huge!

504
00:18:14,111 --> 00:18:15,111
What is that?

505
00:18:15,111 --> 00:18:16,111
I might ask you the same question.

506
00:18:16,111 --> 00:18:17,111
Whoa!

507
00:18:17,111 --> 00:18:18,111
You mean that thing can talk?

508
00:18:18,111 --> 00:18:19,111
I'm not a thing!

509
00:18:19,111 --> 00:18:20,111
I'm a mole!

510
00:18:20,111 --> 00:18:21,111
Mole, you say?

511
00:18:21,111 --> 00:18:22,111
I don't get it.

512
00:18:22,111 --> 00:18:35,111
I'M THE CHAMPION!

513
00:18:35,111 --> 00:18:36,111
You dig?

514
00:18:36,111 --> 00:18:37,111
Great.

515
00:18:37,111 --> 00:18:38,111
Another weirdo.

516
00:18:38,111 --> 00:18:39,111
Champion of what?

517
00:18:39,111 --> 00:18:41,111
You really need to ask?

518
00:18:41,111 --> 00:18:42,871
Great. Another weirdo.

519
00:18:42,871 --> 00:18:44,451
Champion of what?

520
00:18:44,451 --> 00:18:46,751
You really need to ask?

521
00:18:46,751 --> 00:18:49,791
Obviously, I'm the world champion of hole digging.

522
00:18:49,791 --> 00:18:50,991
As crazy as it sounds,

523
00:18:50,991 --> 00:18:53,331
I'm challenging my own record as we speak.

524
00:18:53,331 --> 00:18:56,331
That's no excuse for wrecking the old stilts guy's house.

525
00:18:56,331 --> 00:18:58,471
Where is he supposed to live?

526
00:18:58,471 --> 00:19:00,291
Huh?

527
00:19:00,291 --> 00:19:04,131
What old stilts guy?

528
00:19:08,131 --> 00:19:09,931
They call us a mole.

529
00:19:09,931 --> 00:19:11,331
You like him?

530
00:19:11,331 --> 00:19:12,431
Listen, Li Tanto,

531
00:19:12,431 --> 00:19:15,331
I'm about to go for the world record in stilts standing.

532
00:19:15,331 --> 00:19:16,911
Huh?

533
00:19:16,911 --> 00:19:20,171
It won't be easy, so I may be up there for a few days.

534
00:19:20,171 --> 00:19:23,871
But at least you'll have the mole to keep you company.

535
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:25,651
You can manage while I'm gone, right?

536
00:19:25,651 --> 00:19:28,491
Uh-huh. I'll wait as long as I have to.

537
00:19:28,491 --> 00:19:31,311
But you better come back a champion, okay, Grandpa?

538
00:19:31,311 --> 00:19:33,491
You bet I will. Don't you worry.

539
00:19:33,491 --> 00:19:36,551
I promise I'll make you proud.

540
00:19:36,551 --> 00:19:38,331
It can't be.

541
00:19:38,331 --> 00:19:40,231
It's really you?

542
00:19:40,231 --> 00:19:42,071
Well, of course.

543
00:19:42,071 --> 00:19:42,931
Grandpa!

544
00:19:42,931 --> 00:19:44,431
Li Tanto!

545
00:19:44,431 --> 00:19:46,431
I missed you so much.

546
00:19:46,431 --> 00:19:48,911
I was so lonely without you.

547
00:19:48,911 --> 00:19:50,711
You turned into a fine young man.

548
00:19:50,711 --> 00:19:53,151
I'm so sorry I didn't get to watch you grow up.

549
00:19:53,151 --> 00:19:55,991
I didn't mean to worry you.

550
00:19:55,991 --> 00:19:58,251
I hope you can forgive me.

551
00:19:58,251 --> 00:20:00,951
I didn't see that one coming.

552
00:20:00,951 --> 00:20:04,631
When I thought about how hard my Grandpa was working on his world record,

553
00:20:04,631 --> 00:20:07,491
it inspired me to start on a record of my own.

554
00:20:07,491 --> 00:20:09,251
And suddenly, before I knew it,

555
00:20:09,251 --> 00:20:12,231
all my loneliness turned into a passion for hole digging.

556
00:20:12,231 --> 00:20:13,971
And now you're the champ.

557
00:20:13,971 --> 00:20:17,331
Yup! I'm gonna dig through the whole world!

558
00:20:17,331 --> 00:20:19,731
You ain't big, huh?

559
00:20:19,731 --> 00:20:21,271
Just like the old stilts guy.

560
00:20:21,271 --> 00:20:22,911
Yeah.

561
00:20:22,911 --> 00:20:24,651
That's not a compliment.

562
00:20:24,651 --> 00:20:30,651
Say, couldn't you follow one of your holes to reach the other villagers?

563
00:20:30,651 --> 00:20:31,651
Huh?

564
00:20:31,651 --> 00:20:36,351
Looks like it all worked out, huh?

565
00:20:36,351 --> 00:20:39,731
Yes. I don't know how to thank you for all you've done.

566
00:20:39,731 --> 00:20:42,371
Don't worry about it.

567
00:20:42,371 --> 00:20:43,591
Thanks a lot, ma'am!

568
00:20:43,591 --> 00:20:44,891
If you hadn't said something,

569
00:20:44,891 --> 00:20:48,171
I probably would have been waiting for years to see the other villagers.

570
00:20:51,091 --> 00:20:53,231
Farewell, my friends.

571
00:20:53,231 --> 00:20:55,631
I won't forget you.

572
00:20:55,631 --> 00:20:57,771
Again, thank you so much.

573
00:20:57,771 --> 00:21:00,811
Take care on your way home, old man!

574
00:21:00,811 --> 00:21:02,111
You too!

575
00:21:02,111 --> 00:21:05,511
Wherever you may go, I pray for your safe journey.

576
00:21:06,711 --> 00:21:07,551
That's that.

577
00:21:07,551 --> 00:21:09,351
Time to head off.

578
00:21:09,351 --> 00:21:11,451
Nami, is the log ready yet?

579
00:21:11,451 --> 00:21:12,291
Sure is.

580
00:21:12,291 --> 00:21:13,691
We're all good to go.

581
00:21:13,691 --> 00:21:14,691
All right.

582
00:21:14,691 --> 00:21:16,291
It's about time.

583
00:21:16,291 --> 00:21:17,531
Yeah.

584
00:21:17,531 --> 00:21:18,471
So what now?

585
00:21:18,471 --> 00:21:20,671
Are we gonna snag ourselves a shipwright?

